<!--meta {"lead": "HairPop icons are simple line drawings on a 24-unit grid. They support a label; they rarely replace one.", "description": "Icon style, sizes, labelling rules and the full icon sheet, replacing the text glyphs used in the mocks.", "covers": "Icon grid and stroke, sizes, colour, labelling, the icon sheet, glyph-to-icon mapping"} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Every icon is an inline SVG drawn on a 24×24 grid with a 2px stroke, round caps and round joins, no fill, and <code>stroke: currentColor</code>, so it takes the colour of the text beside it in both themes. Icons are defined once (the <code>ICONS</code> table in <code>build.py</code>, and the matching icon component in the product) and rendered with the <code>.icon</code> class.</p>
  <p>Every page, mock and component writes the icon inline, with nothing else around it: <code>&lt;svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"&gt;&lt;path d="…"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;</code>, where the path is the icon's entry in <code>ICONS</code>, copied verbatim. Size modifiers (<code>icon--sm</code>, <code>icon--lg</code>) and <code>icon--fill</code> go on the same <code>class</code>. There is no sprite sheet, no <code>&lt;use href&gt;</code>, no icon font and no <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>; the product's icon component renders exactly this markup.</p>
  <p>The mocks drew icons with text glyphs (✦, ×, ⌕, !, ✓, →, ★, ⚠, ↑, ↓). Glyphs render differently per font and platform, can be read aloud by screen readers, and do not follow the stroke style. The system replaces each with an SVG icon; see the <a href="#mapping">mapping</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="grid"><h2><a href="#grid">Grid and style</a></h2>
  {{example:The calendar icon at 96px, 24px and 20px. Strokes stay 2 units wide on the 24-unit grid at every size.}}
<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="width: 6rem; height: 6rem; color: var(--color-fg-accent);"><path d="M4 6h16v14H4zM4 10h16M8 3v4M16 3v4"/></svg>
{{icon:calendar|icon--lg}}
{{icon:calendar}}
  {{/example}}
  <ul>
    <li><b>Grid:</b> <code>viewBox="0 0 24 24"</code>; live area 20×20 centred; optical size matched, not mathematical (a circle reaches the live-area edge, a square sits 1 unit inside).</li>
    <li><b>Stroke:</b> 2 units, <code>stroke-linecap: round</code>, <code>stroke-linejoin: round</code>, no fill. <code>.icon--fill</code> exists for the rare solid mark (a filled star in a rating) and is never used for UI controls.</li>
    <li><b>Colour:</b> <code>currentColor</code> only. Status icons get their colour from the component (<code>--alert-icon</code>, <code>--toast-icon</code>), never from the SVG.</li>
    <li><b>Metaphors:</b> one icon means one thing. The sparkle is the brand mark and the styles accent; it never means "new" or "AI".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes"><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2>
  {{example:<code>.icon--sm</code> 16px beside 14px text; <code>.icon</code> 20px beside body text and in buttons (1.25em); <code>.icon--lg</code> 24px for standalone use.}}
<span class="cluster">{{icon:clock|icon--sm}}<small>Small · 16px</small></span>
<span class="cluster">{{icon:clock}}<span>Default · 20px</span></span>
<span class="cluster">{{icon:clock|icon--lg}}<span>Large · 24px</span></span>
  {{/example}}
  <ul>
    <li>Inside a button the icon is <code>1.25em</code>, so it scales with the button size.</li>
    <li>Leave <code>--space-1</code> to <code>--space-2</code> between an icon and its label; buttons and badges set this gap for you.</li>
    <li>Do not scale icons with <code>transform</code>; change the size class so the stroke stays crisp.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sheet"><h2><a href="#sheet">Icon sheet</a></h2>
  <p>Every icon in the system. Names are kebab-case nouns or verbs and never describe shape ("close", not "x").</p>
  <ul class="ds-icons">
