<section class="ds-section" id="mapping"><h2><a href="#mapping">Glyph-to-icon mapping</a></h2>
  <p>Where the mocks used a text glyph, use this icon instead.</p>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Mock glyph</th><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">Icon</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>✦</td><td>Brand in the top bar, style-card art, empty states</td><td>{{icon:sparkle}} <code>sparkle</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>×</td><td>Dialog close, toast and alert dismiss, chip remove (16px, <code>icon--sm</code>, inside a named control)</td><td>{{icon:close}} <code>close</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>⌕</td><td>No-results empty states, the not-found page, search fields</td><td>{{icon:search}} <code>search</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>!</td><td>Error empty states, the service-error page, danger alerts and toasts</td><td>{{icon:alert-circle}} <code>alert-circle</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>✓</td><td>Success empty states, inside the <code>.empty__icon</code> circle that is already drawn</td><td>{{icon:check}} <code>check</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>✓</td><td>Success alerts and toasts (no circle around the icon)</td><td>{{icon:check-circle}} <code>check-circle</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>→</td><td>"Explore Knotless braids →" links (<code>icon--sm</code> inside <code>.link__arrow</code>)</td><td>{{icon:arrow-right}} <code>arrow-right</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>★</td><td>"4.9 ★ from 86 reviews"</td><td>{{icon:star|icon--sm icon--fill}} <code>star</code>, small and filled, the one labelled icon (<code>role="img"</code>, <code>aria-label="out of 5 stars"</code>)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>⚠</td><td>Field error prefix</td><td>{{icon:warning}} <code>warning</code> (the CSS prefix is kept with empty alt text)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>↑ ↓</td><td>Stat deltas</td><td>{{icon:arrow-up|icon--sm}} <code>arrow-up</code>, {{icon:arrow-down|icon--sm}} <code>arrow-down</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>The mock navigation bar's own controls (⌂ all mocks, ☾ dark theme, × hide chrome) are review chrome, not product UI, and keep their glyphs.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="usage"><h2><a href="#usage">Usage</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Pair icons with text. An icon alone is only for universally understood controls (close, menu, more, search) and always has an accessible name.</li>
    <li>Status always combines colour, icon and words: a warning badge says "Awaiting reply"; the icon only reinforces it.</li>
    <li>Do not mix glyphs, emoji or icon fonts with the SVG set.</li>
    <li>Do not rotate or flip an icon to make a new meaning, except chevrons for direction.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss notification">{{icon:close}}</button></div><figcaption>An SVG close icon inside a named button.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss notification">×</button></div><figcaption>A multiplication sign as an icon; its size and weight change with the font.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Decorative icons</b> (next to a visible label) carry <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> and no <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Icon-only controls</b> name the control, not the icon: <code>aria-label="Close dialog"</code>, not "X icon". Add a tooltip with the same words.</li>
    <li><b>Informative standalone icons</b> (the star in "4.9 ★ from 86 reviews") carry <code>role="img"</code> and <code>aria-label="out of 5 stars"</code> on the <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> instead of <code>aria-hidden</code>, so the line reads "4.9 out of 5 stars from 86 reviews". The rating star is the product's only labelled icon.</li>
    <li><b>Contrast:</b> icons that carry meaning reach 3:1 against their background (WCAG 1.4.11); the status icon tokens are checked in <code>contrast-pairs.json</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Forced colours:</b> <code>currentColor</code> follows the system text colour, so icons stay visible in Windows High Contrast.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
